.TH LOGOUT 1
.SH NAME
logout, exit \- end this session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B logout
.br
.B exit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B logout
and
.B exit
are commands built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
The shell ends, with status 0. A login shell's end ends the session: the
terminal shows the login prompt again. A shell started by
.BR su (1)
or another shell returns to the one before.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR login (8),
.BR sh (1)
.SH BUGS
.B exit
takes no status: it is always 0.
